## 1. Das korrigierte Pitch-Skript (Nahtloser Übergang in die Demo)

### Teil A: Das Problem (C-Level Framing & Gartner-Folie)

> *"Every company today is obsessed with collecting more data—more sensor logs, more PDFs, more guidelines. Have you ever looked into an industrial company’s SharePoint? There are multiple versions of safety manuals, conflicting manufacturer datasheets, and nobody knows which one actually applies.*
> *Now, companies throw a standard LLM on top of this mess and hope for magic. **That doesn't solve the chaos—it amplifies it.** Gartner predicts that 60% of AI projects will be abandoned specifically because they lack AI-ready data. Why? Because a standard AI will happily pull a paragraph from an internal SOP, ignore a hardware limit in a sensor datasheet, and give you a confident, completely unreliable answer."*

### Teil B: Die Szene (Exakt euer iMAKS-Szenario: Siegelstation 210 °C vs. 200 °C)

> *"Imagine it’s Sunday morning at a bottling plant. You are the shift supervisor on duty. Suddenly, a temperature warning triggers at the **sealing station**. The lead process engineer is at home with her family. You have minutes to decide: stop the entire bottling line, or keep running?*
> *You check the internal Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)—it clearly states the sealing station should run at up to **210 °C**. A standard RAG chatbot reads this SOP and tells you: 'Everything is fine, keep running up to 210 degrees.'*
> *What the chatbot missed: The temperature sensor installed on that exact station is only rated up to **200 °C** according to the manufacturer's datasheet. Running at 210 °C blinds the sensor and risks hardware failure.*
> *In that moment, **Responsible AI doesn't mean having a polite chatbot.** Responsible AI means making a **defensible, auditable decision** without betting the production line on a blind spot."*

### Teil C: Eure Lösung (Echte Architektur ohne Langfuse)

> *"Let me show you how our system handles this exact bottling line:*
> 1. **Structure before Generation:** *Instead of letting an LLM guess across isolated PDFs, we use a curated Enterprise Digital Twin as a central grounding anchor. It explicitly links the sealing station, its physical sensors, the internal SOPs, and the manufacturer datasheets.*
> 2. **Conflict Escalation, Not Hallucination:** *When our agent traverses the graph for the sealing station, it retrieves both the SOP (210 °C) and the linked sensor datasheet (200 °C). Instead of smoothing over the contradiction, it explicitly flags the conflict to the supervisor. The human stays in control.*
> 3. **Built-in Auditability (No Heavy External Stack):** *We deliberately avoided bloated third-party observability clouds. Every answer directly exposes its **graph traversal path** in the UI—showing each step, reasoning, cited triples, and text passages. And our internal **Audit Log (`/api/audit`)** records every human curation decision, canary test, and operator feedback. Every step is lightweight, local, and 100% traceable."*
